<title>FRANCE: Accor cut debt to 17.5 bln Ffr end-1996.</title>
<headline>Accor cut debt to 17.5 bln Ffr end-1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French hotels group Accor said its net debt stood at 17.5 billion francs at the end of 1996, compared to 25.2 billion in June 1994. It gave no 1995 figure.</p>
<p>Its net debt to equity gearing ratio was below one, the company said in a results statement. The debt reduction was due to hotel property sales.</p>
<p>The company reported a 1996 net attributable profit of 1.06 billion francs, up from 923 million in 1995.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
